  "summary": "Build a half adder from beam A, from the left, and beam B, from below. The Sum detector above must be bright when exactly one beam is on. The Carry detector on the right must be bright only when both are on. You may place one slab of dense glass in the marked region. The score is the lower of the two contrasts, in decibels. Carry is an AND, so the score cannot go much above 6 dB.",
